# Which professor's harness listens on which loopback port.
#
#   cp deploy/users.conf.example deploy/users.conf
#
# One line per person: an account name, whitespace, a port. Blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored. `deploy/users.conf` is not tracked — it
# names the actual people on an actual machine, and that is a deployment fact
# rather than a property of this project.
#
# The name is the OS account, which is also the systemd instance (`dsh@ardak`)
# and the DSH home ($DSH_ROOT/ardak/.dsh). It need NOT be the name the identity
# provider returns; the Caddyfile's map block is where those two are reconciled,
# and keeping that reconciliation in one place is why it is not done here.
#
# The ports are loopback-only and never reachable from outside the machine.
# They are separate anyway, one per person, because they are how the proxy tells
# two professors apart after it has decided which one is asking.
#
# 3080 is deliberately absent: that is what `bin/sample` binds for a single
# local user, and a deployment that reused it would have the shared-laptop
# harness and a professor's fighting over one socket.

# ardak    3101
# aigerim  3102
# nurlan   3103
